clearcote-957: a Windows persona must not keep serving the host's Helvetica on macOS.

MEASURED on the native macOS arm64 build of 150.0.7871.114, platform="windows": every other
macOS-only family was correctly hidden -- Lucida Grande, Menlo, Geneva, Optima, Apple Chancery,
Hiragino Sans all absent -- and `Helvetica Neue` alone still rendered. That makes it a sharper
tell than it would be on a browser that hid nothing: the one macOS font left standing in an
otherwise Windows-shaped font list.

CAUSE. IsBasicFont() waves a short list of families past the cross-OS filter unconditionally.
On a Linux host that is harmless: none of "Helvetica", "Helvetica Neue", "Roboto" or "Sans" is
installed there, and fonts.conf.template maps Helvetica onto Arimo in any case. On macOS,
"Helvetica" and "Helvetica Neue" are genuine system families
(/System/Library/Fonts/Helvetica.ttc and HelveticaNeue.ttc), so the bypass handed a Windows
persona two macOS fonts.

WHAT WINDOWS ANSWERS -- read from the HKLM ...\FontSubstitutes registry key, NOT measured on a
Windows host. Flagged for verification on the next Windows run:
  * "Helvetica" has a substitution entry to Arial which DirectWrite honours, so it is PRESENT
    with Arial's metrics. Resolved here as "Arial", which puts it on the ordinary substitution
    path and lands on Arimo -- the same answer fonts.conf.template gives the Linux build
    (`<match><test name="family">Helvetica</test><edit>Arimo</edit></match>`), so the two
    artifacts still agree.
  * "Helvetica Neue" has no entry and ships with no Windows edition: ABSENT.
The other IsBasicFont names absent from the Windows list -- Roboto, Sans, BlinkMacSystemFont --
are not macOS families either, so they already resolve to nothing and are left on the stock
path.

Scoped to IS_MAC on purpose. The Linux build has the same IsBasicFont bypass; there it is
covered by fonts.conf.template for Helvetica and is a genuine but separate question for
Helvetica Neue, which should be settled with a measurement on the Linux artifact rather than
changed inside a macOS port.

diff -u a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/font_cache.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/font_cache.cc
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/font_cache.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/font_cache.cc
@@ -693,7 +693,39 @@
